{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'define \\\\(jolt-proc|defn proc|defn call' stdlib/jolt/scheme.clj host/gambit/host-statics.ss; sed -n '20,75p' stdlib/jolt/scheme.clj; nl -ba test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh | sed -n '1,100p'; tail -7 build/p1e/run.3TmmZx/stock.stderr; date -u '+%F %T %Z'\"","aggregated_output":"stdlib/jolt/scheme.clj:20:(defn proc\nstdlib/jolt/scheme.clj:26:(defn call\n(defn proc\n  \"The top-level Scheme procedure named by scheme-name (a string), as a\n  callable value. Resolved now; throws when the name is unbound.\"\n  [scheme-name]\n  (jolt.host/scheme-proc scheme-name))\n\n(defn call\n  \"Resolve the top-level Scheme procedure named by scheme-name and apply it\n  to args. Values cross raw — see the namespace docs.\"\n  [scheme-name & args]\n  (apply (jolt.host/scheme-proc scheme-name) args))\n\n(defn eval-string\n  \"Evaluate s as Scheme text — read with the SCHEME reader, not jolt's — and\n  return the last form's value. Definitions persist in the interaction\n  environment.\"\n  [s]\n  (jolt.host/scheme-eval-string s))\n\n(defmacro defsfn\n  \"Def name to the top-level Scheme procedure named by scheme-name:\n  (defsfn fx+ \\\"fx+\\\") then (fx+ 1 2). Resolution happens at load time.\"\n  [name scheme-name]\n  (list 'def name (list 'jolt.scheme/proc scheme-name)))\n\n;; --- (scheme ...): inline Scheme, do-shaped ----------------------------------\n;; The body is READ BY JOLT (the two syntaxes share the s-expression family),\n;; so Scheme spellings jolt's reader rejects are written in jolt spellings and\n;; rendered across: true/false -> #t/#f, \\\\A -> #\\\\A, [1 2 3] -> the datum\n;; vector #(1 2 3), nil -> jolt-nil (the runtime's nil value, a bound host\n;; global). Strings, numbers, and ratios print compatibly. Keywords, maps, and\n;; sets have no Scheme reading and are refused at macroexpansion. Reader sugar\n;; that expands to clojure.core calls (@x, syntax-quote) lands as unbound\n;; Scheme names — write (unquote ...) longhand or avoid it.\n\n(def ^:private scheme-char-names\n  {\\newline \"#\\\\newline\" \\space \"#\\\\space\" \\tab \"#\\\\tab\"\n   \\return \"#\\\\return\" \\backspace \"#\\\\backspace\" \\formfeed \"#\\\\page\"})\n\n(defn- form->scheme\n  \"Render a jolt-read form as Scheme source text. quoted? tracks whether f\n  sits inside (quote ...)/(quasiquote ...) — it decides only how a VECTOR\n  renders: #(...) is a datum, not an expression, in R6RS, so an expression\n  position gets (quote #(...)) and a datum position the bare literal.\n  (unquote ...) under quasiquote re-enters expression position.\"\n  ([f] (form->scheme f false))\n  ([f quoted?]\n   (cond\n     (true? f)    \"#t\"\n     (false? f)   \"#f\"\n     (nil? f)     \"jolt-nil\"\n     (symbol? f)  (str f)\n     (string? f)  (pr-str f)\n     (char? f)    (or (get scheme-char-names f) (str \"#\\\\\" f))\n     (number? f)  (pr-str f)\n     (vector? f)  (let [datum (str \"#(\" (apply str (interpose \" \" (map (fn [x] (form->scheme x true)) f))) \")\")]\n     1\t#!/bin/sh\n     2\t# Capture the stock CLI and then probe each underlying path in a live Yin REPL.\n     3\t# Arguments are absolute paths. Build the bridge and compiled boot first.\n     4\tset -eu\n     5\t\n     6\tgsi=$1\n     7\tdatomworld=$2\n     8\texport JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=$3\n     9\texport JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=1\n    10\trepo=$(CDPATH='' cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\n    11\tcd \"$repo\"\n    12\tmkdir -p build/p1e\n    13\trun=$(mktemp -d \"$repo/build/p1e/run.XXXXXX\")\n    14\techo \"P1e receipts: $run\"\n    15\tmkdir \"$run/store\"\n    16\texport JOLT_P1E_STORE=\"$run/store\"\n    17\t\n    18\tsession() {\n    19\t  name=$1\n    20\t  shift\n    21\t  status=0\n    22\t  started=$(date +%s)\n    23\t  sh \"$repo/host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh\" \"${P1E_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-900}\" \\\n    24\t    \"$gsi\" \"$repo/host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss\" \"$datomworld\" \\\n    25\t    --no-state --index-store \"$@\" >\"$run/$name.stdout\" 2>\"$run/$name.stderr\" || status=$?\n    26\t  echo \"$status\" >\"$run/$name.status\"\n    27\t  cat \"$run/$name.stdout\"\n    28\t  echo \"$name launcher exit $status ($(($(date +%s) - started))s)\"\n    29\t}\n    30\t\n    31\tsession stock \"dht:$JOLT_P1E_STORE\" <<'FORMS'\n    32\t(+ 20 22)\n    33\t(quit)\n    34\tFORMS\n    35\t\n    36\t# Only the entry composition is extended, inside a scratch source root. The\n    37\t# launcher, other host adapters, boot, and Datomworld source stay the same.\n    38\toverlay=\"$run/jolt\"\n    39\tmkdir -p \"$overlay/host/gambit\"\n    40\tcp -R \"$repo/host/gambit/yin\" \"$overlay/host/gambit/yin\"\n    41\tcat \"$repo/test/gambit/fixtures/yin-dht-probe.jolt\" >>\"$overlay/host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt\"\n    42\tfor name in build stdlib jolt-core; do\n    43\t  ln -s \"$repo/$name\" \"$overlay/$name\"\n    44\tdone\n    45\tcd \"$overlay\"\n    46\t\n    47\tsession diagnostics mem <<'FORMS'\n    48\t(+ 20 22)\n    49\t(require 'p1e.probe)\n    50\t(p1e.probe/run :shell-open)\n    51\t(p1e.probe/run :durable-put)\n    52\t(p1e.probe/run :durable-get)\n    53\t(p1e.probe/run :directory-open)\n    54\t(p1e.probe/run :memory-open)\n    55\t(p1e.probe/run :memory-put)\n    56\t(p1e.probe/run :memory-get)\n    57\t(p1e.probe/run :replicate-request)\n    58\t(p1e.probe/run :udp-loopback)\n    59\t(p1e.probe/run :udp-native-load)\n    60\t(p1e.probe/run :c4-control)\n    61\t(p1e.probe/run :close)\n    62\t(+ 40 3)\n    63\t(quit)\n    64\tFORMS\n    65\t\n    66\t# An expected capability refusal is an observation. Missing replies, a crash,\n    67\t# or the watchdog deadline make the evidence run fail.\n    68\ttest \"$(cat \"$run/diagnostics.status\")\" -eq 0\n    69\ttest \"$(cat \"$run/stock.status\")\" -lt 124\n    70\ttest \"$(grep -c '^yin> ' \"$run/diagnostics.stdout\")\" -eq 16\n    71\tgrep -Fx \"yin> 'p1e.probe\" \"$run/diagnostics.stdout\" >/dev/null